1) 从告警标签取 zone，在 Cloudflare Dashboard 的:
1) Take zone from the alert labels and drill down by status code in Analytics in the Cloudflare Dashboard, separating 520-527 (between Cloudflare and the origin) from 500-504 (the origin itself);
2) 52x means an origin connection problem: 521 is the origin refusing the connection and 524 is the origin timing out; curl the origin IP directly and check whether the origin firewall allows Cloudflare's origin fetch ranges;
3) If the 5xx come from the origin, locate them in the origin application logs;
4) As an emergency measure enable Always Online or temporarily point the DNS record at a backup origin.

1) 从告警标签取 zone，在 Dashboard 的 Caching \u0:
1) Take zone from the alert labels and use Caching > Cache Analytics in the Dashboard to see which paths the misses concentrate on;
2) Check whether Page Rules or Cache Rules changed recently; a misconfigured Bypass Cache is the most common cause, so roll the change back first;
3) A change in origin response headers (a new Cache-Control: no-cache or Set-Cookie) also invalidates caching; compare headers before and after the release;
4) If you just ran Purge Everything, the cache is rebuilding as expected; watch whether the hit ratio recovers naturally within a few hours.

1) 从告警标签取 zone，在 Security \u003e Events:
1) Take zone from the alert labels and aggregate Security > Events by source country, ASN, and User-Agent to characterise the attack;
2) Once the pattern is clear, configure a WAF custom rule or rate limiting rule, preferring pattern matching over IP blocking;
3) For high-volume attacks enable Under Attack Mode, bearing in mind it presents a challenge page to legitimate users so the business impact must be assessed;
4) At the same time check whether origin 5xx and response time are affected, and scale the origin first if needed before tuning rules.
